                        id: "l3-2-107",
                        title: "Plumbing Systems Engineering",
                        type: "text",
                        duration: 40,
                        content: `# Plumbing Systems for CEA

## Pipe Materials
**PVC Schedule 40:** 150-200 psi @ 73°F, 33-140°F range, NSF-61 certified
**CPVC:** 200°F max, 100-400 psi, 2-3× PVC cost
**PEX:** -40 to 200°F, 160 psi, freeze resistant, flexible
**ABS:** DWV only (not pressure), impact resistant

## Flow Calculations
**Q = A × V** (Flow = Area × Velocity)
**Optimal Velocities:** Suction 2-4 fps | Pressure 4-8 fps | Drain 2-3 fps

**Pipe Sizing:** For 500 GPM @ 6 fps → Use 6" Schedule 40 PVC

**Hazen-Williams Friction Loss:**
**hf = (4.52 × L × Q^1.85) / (C^1.85 × d^4.87)**
C=150 for PVC
**Example:** 100 ft of 2" PVC @ 50 GPM = 3.8 ft head loss

## Fittings

**Solvent Welding:** Cut square → Deburr → Dry-fit → Prime → Cement → Hold 30s → Cure 2 hrs
**Temperature:** 40-110°F ambient | Full cure: 24 hrs

**Threaded (NPT):** Teflon tape 3-4 wraps clockwise + hand-tight + 1-2 turns

**Bulkheads:** Drill 1/8" oversized → Deburr → Insert → Gaskets both sides → Hand-tight + 1/4 turn

## Valves
**Ball:** On/off, 90° turn, minimal pressure drop
**Check:** Prevent backflow, 0.5-5 psi cracking pressure
**Float:** Auto-fill, toilet-style or livestock waterer

## Code Compliance
**Potable Water:** NSF-61 materials, backflow prevention (air gap 6" or RPZ valve)
**Drainage:** 1/4" per foot slope min, venting required >40 ft runs
**Pressure Rating:** Design for 0.5× rated pressure (safety factor 2.0)

**Example:** Schedule 40 PVC rated 280 psi → Design for 140 psi max

## Components
**Uniseals:** Flexible penetrations, <10 psi, 1/2"-4" sizes
**True Union:** Removable valves without cutting
**Swing Joints:** Adjustable connections for floating components

## Water Hammer Prevention
**Causes:** Sudden valve closure, pump shutdown
**Solutions:** Slow-close valves, surge tanks, air chambers

## Installation
**Support Spacing:** 1/2"-3/4": 32" | 1"-2": 48" | 3"-4": 60" | 6"+: 72"

**Thermal Expansion (PVC):** ΔL = α × L × ΔT (α = 3×10⁻⁵ in/in/°F)
**Example:** 100 ft, 50°F swing = 1.8" expansion → Use expansion loops

**Slope:** 1/4" per foot drainage | Vent high points | Drain low points

## Testing
**Pressure Test:** 1.5× working pressure, hold 2 hrs, <5% pressure drop acceptable
**Flow Test:** Verify rates, valve operation, leak check

**References:** UPC, IPC, NSF/ANSI 61`
