                lessons: [
                    { id: "l7-1-201", title: "Hiring Growers", type: "video", duration: 15, videoUrl: "https://example.com/placeholder" },
                    { id: "l7-2-201", title: "Building Your Team", type: "text", duration: 25, content: `# Staff Management for Commercial Farms

## Hiring the Right People

### Key Positions

**Head Grower / Farm Manager**
- Overall production responsibility
- Technical expertise
- Problem-solving ability
- Leadership skills

**Production Workers**
- Seeding, transplanting, harvesting
- Attention to detail
- Physical stamina
- Reliability > experience

**Harvest/Pack Team**
- Speed and accuracy
- Food safety awareness
- Quality consciousness
- Often part-time/seasonal

### Where to Find Workers

- Agricultural job boards (AgCareers)
- Local community colleges
- Farm labor contractors
- Referrals from current staff
- Social media/Craigslist
- Workforce development programs

### Hiring Process

1. **Clear job description** - Specific duties, hours, pay
2. **Working interview** - See them actually work
3. **Reference checks** - Actually call them
4. **Trial period** - 30-90 days probationary

### Red Flags

- Unreliable transportation
- Can't pass background check (if required)
- Poor attendance history
- Attitude issues in interview
- Overqualified (won't stay)

## Compensation

### Wages
| Position | Typical Range |
|----------|---------------|
| Entry worker | $12-16/hour |
| Skilled worker | $15-20/hour |
| Team lead | $18-25/hour |
| Farm manager | $45-75K salary |

### Benefits (if affordable)
- Health insurance
- Paid time off
- Produce allowance
- Flexible scheduling
- Training/development` },
                    { id: "l7-3-201", title: "Training & Retention", type: "text", duration: 20, content: `# Training and Keeping Good Staff

## Training Systems

### Onboarding (Week 1)
- Farm tour and orientation
- Safety training (required)
- Meet the team
- Basic SOPs
- Shadow experienced worker

### Skills Training (Weeks 2-4)
- Specific task training
- Practice with supervision
- Gradual independence
- Competency checklists

### Ongoing Development
- Cross-training on multiple tasks
- Leadership development
- Industry conferences/events
- Skill certifications

## Training Best Practices

**"Tell, Show, Do, Review"**

1. **Tell** - Explain what and why
2. **Show** - Demonstrate the task
3. **Do** - Have them try it
4. **Review** - Feedback and correction

## Retention Strategies

**Why people leave:**
- Low pay
- No advancement
- Poor management
- Lack of appreciation
- Better opportunities

**Why people stay:**
- Fair compensation
- Respect and recognition
- Learning opportunities
- Good team/culture
- Mission alignment

### Practical Retention Tactics

1. **Regular feedback** - Monthly check-ins
2. **Recognition** - Celebrate wins publicly
3. **Growth paths** - Clear advancement opportunities
4. **Involve in decisions** - Ask for input
5. **Competitive pay** - Annual reviews
6. **Good culture** - Team meals, events
7. **Flexibility** - When possible

## Safety Culture

**Required training:**
- Chemical handling (if applicable)
- Electrical safety
- Lifting techniques
- Emergency procedures
- First aid/CPR (key personnel)

**Safety equipment:**
- Appropriate footwear
- Gloves for specific tasks
- Eye protection (chemicals)
- Hearing protection (if needed)

**Report all injuries immediately!**` },
                    { id: "l7-4-201", title: "Staff Quiz", type: "quiz", duration: 10, questions: [
                        { id: "q1", question: "What's the recommended training approach?", options: ["Sink or swim", "Tell, Show, Do, Review", "Video training only", "Written manuals only"], correctAnswer: 1 }
                    ]}
                ]
