                        content: `# Suffocation Strategy

Horticultural oils kill by physical means - no chemical resistance possible.

## Types of Oils

| Oil Type | Viscosity | Use Season | Notes |
|----------|-----------|------------|-------|
| **Dormant** | Heavy | Winter | Trees only, high rates |
| **Summer/Supreme** | Light | Growing season | Safe on green tissue |
| **Narrow-range** | Very refined | Anytime | Lowest phyto risk |

For greenhouse use, always choose summer/narrow-range oils.

## Mode of Action

\`\`\`
Primary: Suffocation
- Oil coats insect body
- Blocks spiracles (breathing pores)
- Insect suffocates within hours

Secondary: Disruption
- Disrupts feeding
- Damages egg shells
- Blocks pheromone reception
\`\`\`

## Target Spectrum

| Excellent | Good | Poor |
|-----------|------|------|
| Scale insects | Aphids | Adult beetles |
| Mealybugs | Whiteflies | Caterpillars |
| Spider mites | Thrips | Flying insects |
| Eggs (many species) | | |

## Application Guidelines

\`\`\`
Rates:
- General: 1-2% (2.5-5 oz/gallon)
- Spider mites: 1%
- Scale/mealybug: 2%
- Eggs: 2%

Coverage:
- Complete coverage mandatory
- Oil must contact pest
- No residual activity
\`\`\`

## Safety Considerations

| Condition | Risk | Recommendation |
|-----------|------|----------------|
| Temperature >90°F | High phytotoxicity | Don't apply |
| Temperature <40°F | Poor spreading | Don't apply |
| High humidity | Slow drying | Caution |
| Sulfur within 30 days | Severe burn | Avoid combo |
| Drought-stressed plants | Phytotoxicity | Water first |

## Products

| Product | Type | Notes |
|---------|------|-------|
| SuffOil-X | Mineral oil | OMRI, very refined |
| JMS Stylet Oil | Mineral oil | Extra refined |
| Trilogy | Neem oil | Oil + azadirachtin |
| Pure Spray Green | Mineral | Food-grade |

## Fish Safety in Aquaponics

\`\`\`
⚠️ CAUTION: Oils can form surface film on water

Prevention:
- Apply only to plant canopy
- Avoid drip into fish systems
- Use targeted spray, not drenching
- Good in DWC/NFT with contained root zones
\`\`\``
