                        content: `# Seasonal Planning

Pest pressure follows predictable patterns - plan accordingly.

## Seasonal Pest Pressure (Northern Hemisphere)

| Season | Primary Threats | Focus Areas |
|--------|----------------|-------------|
| **Winter** | Fungus gnats, scale | Monitor, prevent |
| **Spring** | Aphids, thrips | Ramp up scouting, beneficials |
| **Summer** | Mites, whiteflies | Peak pressure, active management |
| **Fall** | Whiteflies, caterpillars | Wind-down, cleanup |

## Monthly Task Calendar

\`\`\`
JANUARY
□ Review previous year's records
□ Update IPM plan
□ Order supplies for spring
□ Deep clean during low production

FEBRUARY
□ Install fresh sticky traps
□ Repair screens, seals
□ Train new staff on protocols
□ Baseline beneficial releases

MARCH
□ Increase scouting frequency
□ Begin preventive beneficials
□ Watch for early aphid flights
□ Inspect incoming plant material

APRIL
□ Peak aphid/thrips pressure begins
□ Weekly beneficial releases
□ Review thresholds - adjust if needed
□ Document any resistant populations

MAY
□ Transition to summer pest focus
□ Spider mite prevention begins
□ Evaluate biological control efficacy
□ Mid-season supply order

JUNE-AUGUST
□ Maximum scouting frequency
□ Watch for mite outbreaks
□ Maintain beneficials program
□ Document all treatments

SEPTEMBER
□ Watch for fall pest migrations
□ Evaluate season effectiveness
□ Begin reducing inputs
□ Plan fall cleanup

OCTOBER-NOVEMBER
□ Thorough facility cleanup
□ Crop-free period if possible
□ Repair infrastructure
□ Update equipment

DECEMBER
□ Compile annual records
□ Calculate costs/effectiveness
□ Plan next year's program
□ Research new methods
\`\`\`

## Key Timing Events

| Event | IPM Action |
|-------|------------|
| New crop introduction | Quarantine, inspect, treat if needed |
| Season change | Adjust monitoring frequency |
| Staff changeover | Retrain, review protocols |
| After outbreak | Root cause analysis, plan update |
| Certification audit | Records review, documentation check |`
