                        content: `# The Cold Water Workhorse

Rainbow trout (Oncorhynchus mykiss) is the most commonly cultured cold water fish.

## Growth Performance

| Parameter | Value |
|-----------|-------|
| Optimal temp | 54-60°F (12-16°C) |
| Growth rate | 0.5-1% body weight/day |
| Time to 1 lb | 12-14 months |
| Time to 2 lbs | 18-24 months |
| FCR | 1.0-1.4:1 (excellent!) |
| Maximum size | 20+ lbs (4-5 years) |

## Commercial Strains

| Strain | Characteristics |
|--------|-----------------|
| **Kamloops** | Fast growth, large size |
| **Shasta** | Disease resistant |
| **Troutlodge** | Commercial standard, consistent |
| **Steelhead** | Sea-run form, larger |
| **Golden** | Color variant, niche market |

## Feed Requirements

\`\`\`
Protein levels by size:

Fry: 50-55% protein
Fingerlings: 45-50%
Growout: 40-45%
Broodstock: 38-42%

Fat content: 15-20% (higher than tilapia)

Key micronutrients:
- Astaxanthin (for pink flesh color)
- Vitamin E (stress resistance)
- Vitamin C (immune function)
\`\`\`

## Market Sizes

| Size Class | Weight | Primary Market |
|------------|--------|----------------|
| Pan-size | 10-12 oz | Restaurant whole fish |
| Plate-size | 1-1.5 lbs | Restaurant/retail |
| Steelhead-size | 2-4 lbs | Retail fillets |
| Trophy | 5+ lbs | Stocking, specialty |

## Production Calendar

\`\`\`
Year 1:
Month 1-3: Fingerling stage (2-4")
Month 4-8: Juvenile growth (0.1-0.3 lb)
Month 9-12: Approach pan-size (0.5-0.75 lb)

Year 2:
Month 13-18: Plate/retail size (1-2 lb)
Month 19-24: Large fillets (2-4 lb)
\`\`\`

## Disease Considerations

Common trout diseases:

| Disease | Cause | Prevention |
|---------|-------|------------|
| IHN | Virus | Certified fingerlings, quarantine |
| Furunculosis | Bacteria | Water quality, avoid stress |
| Ich | Parasite | Salt treatment, quarantine |
| Columnaris | Bacteria | Keep temps below 65°F |

**Stress is the #1 disease trigger** - handle gently!`
