                        content: `# Maximizing Barramundi Growth

Fast growth is barramundi's competitive advantage.

## Growth Performance

\`\`\`
Growth Curve (at optimal conditions):

Month 1: 1 gram → 15 grams
Month 3: 15 grams → 100 grams
Month 6: 100 grams → 400 grams (0.9 lb)
Month 10: 400 grams → 700 grams (1.5 lb)
Month 18: 700 grams → 1.5 kg (3.3 lb)

Growth rate: 2-3 grams/day at optimal
\`\`\`

## Feed Requirements

| Life Stage | Protein % | Fat % | Feed Size |
|------------|-----------|-------|-----------|
| Fry | 50-55% | 12-14% | 0.3-0.8mm |
| Fingerling | 45-50% | 10-12% | 1.0-2.0mm |
| Juvenile | 42-45% | 10-12% | 3-5mm |
| Growout | 38-42% | 12-16% | 6-10mm |

## Feeding Strategy

\`\`\`
Feeding frequency by size:

Fry: 8-10x daily (auto-feeder recommended)
Fingerling: 4-6x daily
Juvenile: 3-4x daily
Growout: 2-3x daily

Feed to satiation:
- Watch for active feeding behavior
- Stop when interest wanes
- Remove uneaten feed
- Track consumption rates
\`\`\`

## FCR Expectations

| Condition | FCR |
|-----------|-----|
| Optimal RAS | 1.2-1.4:1 |
| Good management | 1.4-1.6:1 |
| Suboptimal | 1.6-2.0:1 |

**Excellent efficiency** - among best for carnivorous fish.

## Feed Training

\`\`\`
Barramundi train to pellet easily:

Week 1: Live artemia/rotifers
Week 2: Mix live + dry crumble
Week 3: Mostly dry crumble
Week 4: Full pellet diet

Key success factors:
- Multiple small feedings
- Consistent timing
- Temperature 82-86°F
- Adequate stocking density (feeding competition)
\`\`\`

## Harvest Planning

| Market | Target Weight | Time | Price/lb |
|--------|---------------|------|----------|
| Pan-size | 0.75-1.0 lb | 8-10 months | $8-10 |
| Plate | 1.5-2.0 lb | 12-14 months | $10-12 |
| Fillet | 2.5-3.5 lb | 18-24 months | $12-15 |`
