                        content: `# What's In Fish Feed?

Understanding ingredients helps evaluate feed quality.

## Protein Sources

| Ingredient | Protein % | Quality | Cost |
|------------|-----------|---------|------|
| Fish meal | 60-72% | Excellent | $$$ |
| Soybean meal | 44-48% | Good | $ |
| Poultry meal | 58-65% | Good | $$ |
| Blood meal | 80-85% | Good | $$ |
| Insect meal | 55-65% | Very good | $$$ |
| Single-cell protein | 45-75% | Good | $$$ |

## The Fish Meal Dilemma

\`\`\`
Fish meal is ideal but:
- Expensive
- Sustainability concerns
- Price volatility
- Limited supply

Modern feeds reduce fish meal:
- 50% fish meal (traditional)
- 15-25% fish meal (current)
- 0-10% fish meal (sustainable/organic)

Replacement strategies:
- Soy protein concentrate
- Insect meal (BSF larvae)
- Single-cell protein
- Plant protein blends
\`\`\`

## Fat/Oil Sources

| Source | Omega-3 | Omega-6 | Use |
|--------|---------|---------|-----|
| Fish oil | High | Low | Cold water fish |
| Poultry fat | Low | Moderate | Warm water fish |
| Soybean oil | Low | High | Economy feeds |
| Algae oil | High | Low | Omega-3 supplement |

## Carbohydrate Sources

| Ingredient | Function |
|------------|----------|
| Wheat | Binder, energy |
| Corn | Energy, binder |
| Rice bran | Energy |
| Tapioca | Binder |

**Note**: Fish can't digest carbs efficiently (use <25% of diet)

## Key Additives

\`\`\`
Essential additives:

VITAMINS
- Vitamin C (immune function)
- Vitamin E (antioxidant)
- B vitamins (metabolism)

MINERALS
- Phosphorus (bones)
- Calcium (bones, shells)
- Trace minerals (enzymes)

OTHER
- Attractants (improve palatability)
- Binders (pellet integrity)
- Antioxidants (prevent rancidity)
- Pigments (color in flesh/scales)
\`\`\``
