                        content: `# Fish Enterprise Budget: Tilapia Example

Fish production has different cost structures than crops - let's build a complete budget.

## Production Assumptions

| Metric | Value | Notes |
|--------|-------|-------|
| Tank capacity | 3,000 gallons total | 4 tanks × 750 gal |
| Stocking density | 0.5 lb/gal at harvest | Conservative |
| Harvest weight | 1.25 lbs each | Market size |
| Production cycles | 2.5/year | ~150 day cycle |
| Fingerling survival | 85% | 15% mortality |
| FCR | 1.5 | 1.5 lbs feed per lb gain |

## Annual Production

\`\`\`
3,000 gal × 0.5 lb/gal × 2.5 cycles = 3,750 lbs/year
At 85% survival rate = 3,188 marketable lbs
\`\`\`

## Revenue

| Channel | % | Price/lb | Revenue |
|---------|---|----------|---------|
| Live sales | 30% | $6.00 | $5,739 |
| Whole fresh | 40% | $5.00 | $6,376 |
| Filleted | 30% | $8.00 (yield 33%) | $8,501* |
| **Weighted** | 100% | | **$20,616** |

*Fillet revenue: 3,188 × 30% × 0.33 yield × $8.00 × 3.33 (markup factor)

## Variable Costs

| Item | Cost | Units | Annual |
|------|------|-------|--------|
| Fingerlings | $0.35 each | 3,750 | $1,313 |
| Feed (35% protein) | $0.45/lb | 4,782 lbs | $2,152 |
| Processing labor | $2.00/lb fillet | 315 lbs | $630 |
| Packaging | $0.50/unit | 1,200 | $600 |
| Salt/additives | $20/month | 12 | $240 |
| Ice | $15/month | 12 | $180 |
| **Total Variable** | | | **$5,115** |

**Variable Cost per lb: $1.60**

## Fixed Cost Allocation

| Fixed Cost | Annual | % to Fish | Allocated |
|------------|--------|-----------|-----------|
| Tank depreciation | $1,200 | 100% | $1,200 |
| Aeration equipment | $600 | 100% | $600 |
| Heating (tropical) | $2,400 | 100% | $2,400 |
| Labor (fish care) | $6,000 | 100% | $6,000 |
| Testing supplies | $480 | 100% | $480 |
| **Total Fixed** | | | **$10,680** |

**Fixed Cost per lb: $3.35**

## Profitability Summary

| Metric | Per Pound | Annual |
|--------|-----------|--------|
| Revenue | $6.47 | $20,616 |
| Variable Costs | $1.60 | $5,115 |
| **Contribution Margin** | $4.87 | $15,501 |
| Fixed Costs | $3.35 | $10,680 |
| **Net Profit** | $1.52 | **$4,821** |

**Profit Margin: 23.4%**

## Fish vs Crops Comparison

| Metric | Tilapia | Butterhead Lettuce |
|--------|---------|-------------------|
| Annual Revenue | $20,616 | $164,746 |
| Net Profit | $4,821 | $76,896 |
| Profit Margin | 23.4% | 46.7% |
| Capital Required | Higher | Lower |
| Labor Intensity | Lower | Higher |
| Risk Level | Higher | Lower |

## Key Insight

Fish typically generate lower margins but provide the nutrient engine for the higher-margin crop production. The true value of fish in aquaponics extends beyond direct sales.`
