                        content: `# Managing Seasonal Fluctuations

Even controlled-environment farms experience seasonal patterns that affect cash flow.

## Revenue Seasonality

### Demand Patterns
| Season | Restaurant | Farmers Market | Grocery | Overall |
|--------|------------|----------------|---------|---------|
| **Winter** | Moderate | Very Low | Steady | 70% |
| **Spring** | High | Building | Steady | 100% |
| **Summer** | Lower (closed) | Peak | Steady | 95% |
| **Fall** | High | Declining | Steady | 110% |

### Price Patterns
| Season | Local Premium | Competition | Your Pricing |
|--------|---------------|-------------|--------------|
| **Winter** | Highest | Lowest | Premium pricing |
| **Spring** | High | Building | Strong pricing |
| **Summer** | Low | Highest | Competitive |
| **Fall** | Moderate | Declining | Rebuilding |

## Expense Seasonality

### Utility Costs
| Season | Heating | Cooling | Lighting | Total |
|--------|---------|---------|----------|-------|
| **Winter** | High | None | High | Peak |
| **Spring** | Moderate | Low | Moderate | Average |
| **Summer** | None | High | Low | Moderate |
| **Fall** | Low | Low | Moderate | Lowest |

### Labor Patterns
| Season | Production | Harvest | Deliveries | Total |
|--------|------------|---------|------------|-------|
| **Winter** | Steady | Lower | Lower | 80% |
| **Spring** | Peak | Building | Growing | 110% |
| **Summer** | Steady | Peak | Moderate | 105% |
| **Fall** | Steady | High | Peak | 105% |

## The Cash Flow Mismatch

### The Problem
\`\`\`
Winter: Low revenue + High utility costs = Cash crisis
Summer: Revenue ok + Low costs = Cash builds
\`\`\`

### Solutions

1. **Build reserves in summer/fall** for winter survival
2. **Pre-sell winter CSA shares** in fall
3. **Negotiate seasonal payment terms** with vendors
4. **Diversify products** to smooth revenue

## Monthly Cash Reserve Target

| Risk Level | Reserve Target |
|------------|----------------|
| Conservative | 3 months expenses |
| Moderate | 2 months expenses |
| Aggressive | 1 month expenses |
| Danger Zone | < 1 month |

## Seasonal Planning Calendar

| Month | Revenue Focus | Expense Focus | Cash Strategy |
|-------|--------------|---------------|---------------|
| Jan | Restaurant push | Cut discretionary | Preserve |
| Feb | Indoor events | Negotiate utilities | Preserve |
| Mar | Market season prep | Buy early inputs | Invest |
| Apr | Market launch | Hire seasonal | Invest |
| May | Peak marketing | Full operations | Build |
| Jun | CSA renewal | Review contracts | Build |
| Jul | Farm tours | Mid-year review | Build |
| Aug | Fall pre-sales | Prepare for school | Build |
| Sep | Restaurant refresh | Winter prep | Maximum build |
| Oct | Holiday marketing | Stock supplies | Build |
| Nov | Gift sales | Reduce hours | Preserve |
| Dec | Maintenance | Plan next year | Preserve |`
