                        id: "l4-2-209",
                        title: "Competitor Research",
                        type: "text",
                        duration: 20,
                        content: `# Know Your Competition

Understanding competitors helps you find gaps, differentiate, and price appropriately.

## Who Are Your Competitors?

### Direct Competitors
Farms selling similar products to similar customers:
- Other aquaponic/hydroponic farms
- Local soil-based farms
- Regional greenhouses

### Indirect Competitors
Alternative ways customers solve the same problem:
- Grocery store produce section
- Meal kit services
- Restaurant supply distributors
- Frozen/processed vegetables

### Substitute Products
Different products that serve similar needs:
- Imported organic produce
- Home gardens
- Preserved/canned options

## Competitor Intelligence Gathering

### Public Information
| Source | What You Learn |
|--------|----------------|
| Farmers markets | Products, prices, volume, presentation |
| Social media | Marketing approach, customer engagement |
| Restaurant menus | Who supplies them, prices charged |
| Grocery displays | Shelf space, pricing, brands |
| News/press | Expansion plans, challenges |

### Network Intelligence
- Talk to chefs about supplier pros/cons
- Ask market managers about vendor performance
- Join grower associations
- Attend industry events

## Competitive Analysis Template

### For Each Major Competitor

| Factor | Competitor A | Competitor B | You |
|--------|--------------|--------------|-----|
| Products | Lettuce, tomatoes | Microgreens | Full range |
| Quality | Good | Premium | Premium |
| Price point | Low | High | Mid-high |
| Delivery | Yes | No | Yes |
| Capacity | High | Low | Medium |
| Reputation | Established | Niche | New |
| Weaknesses | Inconsistent | Limited volume | Unproven |

## Finding Your Competitive Advantage

### Possible Differentiators

| Advantage Type | Examples |
|---------------|----------|
| **Product** | Unique varieties, superior quality, year-round |
| **Service** | Better delivery, custom orders, responsiveness |
| **Price** | Lower cost structure, better value |
| **Relationship** | Personal connection, transparency, farm visits |
| **Story** | Mission-driven, sustainability, local ownership |

### Sustainable Advantages

Strong advantages are hard to copy:
- Built-in cost advantages (location, scale)
- Exclusive relationships
- Proprietary methods or varieties
- Reputation built over time

Weak advantages are easily copied:
- Marketing messaging
- Packaging
- Price cuts
- Product selection

## Competitive Response Planning

What will competitors do when you enter?
- Ignore you (you're too small to matter)
- Match your prices
- Increase marketing
- Lock up key customers
- Nothing (they're not paying attention)`
