                        duration: 20,
                        content: `# Staying Legal: Registrations and Compliance

Running a farm business requires various registrations at federal, state, and local levels.

## Federal Requirements

| Registration | Who Needs It | Purpose |
|--------------|--------------|---------|
| **EIN (Tax ID)** | All businesses with employees or LLCs | Federal tax identification |
| **Farm Number** | Anyone seeking USDA programs | FSA tracking |
| **Organic Certification** | If labeling as organic | USDA NOP compliance |

## State Requirements

| Registration | Typical Requirements | Cost Range |
|--------------|---------------------|------------|
| **Business Registration** | File articles with Secretary of State | $50-500 |
| **Annual Report** | Confirm business info yearly | $0-100 |
| **Sales Tax Permit** | If selling taxable items | Usually free |
| **Employer Registration** | If you have employees | Free |
| **Nursery License** | If selling live plants | $25-200 |
| **Aquaculture License** | For fish production | Varies by state |

## Local Requirements

| Registration | Notes |
|--------------|-------|
| **Business License** | City or county registration |
| **Zoning Approval** | Agricultural zone or special use |
| **Building Permits** | For new construction |
| **Health Department** | If processing or preparing food |
| **Fire Inspection** | For commercial facilities |

## Farm-Specific Registrations

### Food Safety
| Registration | When Needed |
|--------------|-------------|
| **Produce Safety Rule** | If selling covered produce |
| **Preventive Controls** | If processing/manufacturing |
| **GAP Certification** | For retail/wholesale channels |

### Water Rights
| Issue | Varies By |
|-------|-----------|
| Water use permits | State water law |
| Discharge permits | EPA/state environmental |
| Well permits | Local requirements |

## Compliance Calendar

| Month | Task |
|-------|------|
| January | Annual report filing (check state) |
| March | Review insurance renewals |
| April | File taxes (or extension) |
| June | Mid-year compliance review |
| October | Prepare year-end documents |
| December | Renew licenses expiring year-end |

## Staying Organized

### Document Retention

| Document Type | Keep For |
|---------------|----------|
| Tax returns | 7 years minimum |
| Employee records | 7 years after termination |
| Contracts | Duration + 7 years |
| Entity documents | Permanently |
| Insurance policies | 10 years after expiration |
| Food safety records | 2-3 years (per program) |

### Compliance Systems
- Calendar reminders for renewals
- Central filing system (digital preferred)
- Professional relationships (attorney, accountant)
- Industry association membership for updates`
