                        content: `# Setting Up Your Farm Accounting

A well-organized chart of accounts makes financial tracking and tax preparation much easier.

## What is a Chart of Accounts?

A chart of accounts is the complete list of all accounts used to record financial transactions. Think of it as the filing system for your money.

## Account Categories

| Category | Type | Examples |
|----------|------|----------|
| **Assets** | What you own | Cash, equipment, inventory |
| **Liabilities** | What you owe | Loans, accounts payable |
| **Equity** | Owner's stake | Owner investment, retained earnings |
| **Revenue** | Money earned | Sales, grants, other income |
| **Expenses** | Money spent | Seeds, labor, utilities |

## Farm-Specific Chart of Accounts

### Assets (1000s)
\`\`\`
1000 - Cash/Checking
1010 - Savings Account
1100 - Accounts Receivable
1200 - Inventory - Growing Crops
1210 - Inventory - Harvested Crops
1220 - Inventory - Fish
1230 - Inventory - Supplies
1300 - Prepaid Expenses
1500 - Equipment
1510 - Accumulated Depreciation - Equipment
1600 - Greenhouse/Buildings
1610 - Accumulated Depreciation - Buildings
\`\`\`

### Liabilities (2000s)
\`\`\`
2000 - Accounts Payable
2100 - Credit Card Payable
2200 - Line of Credit
2300 - Equipment Loans
2400 - Mortgage/Real Estate Loans
2500 - Customer Deposits (prepaid CSA)
2600 - Payroll Liabilities
\`\`\`

### Revenue (4000s)
\`\`\`
4000 - Produce Sales - Wholesale
4010 - Produce Sales - Retail/Market
4020 - Produce Sales - Restaurant
4100 - Fish Sales
4200 - CSA Revenue
4300 - Grant Income
4400 - Workshop/Tour Income
4900 - Other Income
\`\`\`

### Expenses (5000-6000s)
\`\`\`
5000 - Seeds and Seedlings
5010 - Growing Media
5020 - Fish Feed
5030 - Fingerlings
5040 - Packaging and Supplies
5100 - Labor - Production
5110 - Labor - Sales/Delivery
5120 - Payroll Taxes
5200 - Utilities - Electric
5210 - Utilities - Water
5220 - Utilities - Propane/Gas
5300 - Rent
5400 - Insurance
5500 - Equipment Maintenance
5600 - Marketing
5700 - Professional Services
5800 - Depreciation
5900 - Interest Expense
\`\`\`

## Account Numbering Best Practices

| Principle | Example |
|-----------|---------|
| Leave gaps | 5000, 5010, 5020 (room to add 5005) |
| Group logically | All utilities start with 52XX |
| Be consistent | Once you pick a system, stick to it |
| Keep it simple | Don't over-complicate initially |`
