                        duration: 15,
                        content: `# Choosing and Using Accounting Software

Good systems save time and provide insights. Bad systems create frustration and errors.

## Software Options

| Software | Cost | Best For |
|----------|------|----------|
| **QuickBooks Online** | $25-80/mo | Most small farms |
| **Wave** | Free | Very simple needs |
| **FreshBooks** | $17-55/mo | Service-focused |
| **Xero** | $13-70/mo | Multi-currency, advanced |
| **Spreadsheets** | Free | Minimal transactions |

## QuickBooks for Farms

### Setup Essentials
1. Import chart of accounts (customize for farming)
2. Connect bank accounts for automatic import
3. Set up products/services for each item sold
4. Create customer list
5. Create vendor list
6. Enable inventory tracking if needed

### Key Features to Use
| Feature | Purpose |
|---------|---------|
| Bank Rules | Automatically categorize recurring transactions |
| Invoice Templates | Professional billing for wholesale customers |
| Recurring Transactions | Monthly expenses like rent |
| Reports | P&L, Balance Sheet, Sales by Customer |
| Classes | Track by enterprise (lettuce, fish, CSA) |

## Daily/Weekly Habits

### Daily (5 minutes)
- Record cash sales
- File receipts (photo with phone)

### Weekly (30 minutes)
- Categorize bank transactions
- Send invoices
- Follow up on receivables

### Monthly (2-3 hours)
- Reconcile bank accounts
- Review P&L
- Compare actual vs budget
- Prepare sales tax if applicable

## Integration with Farm Management

| Data Source | How to Connect |
|-------------|----------------|
| POS system | Many integrate with QuickBooks |
| CSA software | May export sales data |
| Payroll | Often integrated service |
| Bank/credit cards | Automatic import |

## Working with Professionals

### When to Get Help
- Initial setup
- Year-end tax preparation
- Quarterly review
- When you're confused

### What to Prepare
- Bank statements reconciled
- Receipts organized
- Questions written down
- Access credentials shared securely

## Red Flags in Your Books

| Warning Sign | What It Might Mean |
|--------------|-------------------|
| Uncategorized transactions | Falling behind |
| Negative bank balance in system | Timing or reconciliation issue |
| COGS higher than revenue | Serious pricing problem |
| Big "Other" category | Not tracking properly |`
