                        type: "text",
                        duration: 25,
                        content: `# Comparing Greenhouse Heating Technologies

Each heating system has advantages for different situations. Many greenhouses use multiple systems together.

## System Comparison

| System | Efficiency | Capital Cost | Operating Cost | Best For |
|--------|------------|--------------|----------------|----------|
| Unit heaters (gas) | 80-93% | Low | Medium | Small houses |
| Hot water boiler | 85-95% | High | Medium | Large operations |
| Radiant tube | 90-95% | Medium | Low-Medium | Uniform heat |
| Biomass boiler | 70-85% | High | Low | Fuel cost savings |
| Heat pump | 300-400% COP | Very high | Low | Mild climates |
| Geothermal | 400-500% COP | Very high | Very low | Long-term investment |

## Forced Air vs. Radiant Heat

**Forced Air (Unit Heaters):**
- Pros: Low cost, quick response, good air circulation
- Cons: Temperature stratification, drying effect, direct draft on plants
- Placement: Wall-mounted, blow across bench tops

**Radiant Heat (Infrared Tubes, Hot Water Pipes):**
- Pros: Uniform heat, heats surfaces directly, energy efficient
- Cons: Higher capital cost, slower response
- Placement: Overhead (IR tubes), under-bench (hot water)

## Root Zone Heating

Heating the growing medium saves energy and improves growth:

| System | Heat Delivery | Benefits |
|--------|--------------|----------|
| Hot water pipes | In-bench or below | Uniform, reliable |
| Electric cables | In growing medium | Precise control, zoning |
| Hot water mats | Under containers | Flexible, movable |

Energy savings: Root zone heating can reduce air temperature 5-10°F while maintaining same growth.

## Fuel Considerations

| Fuel | BTU/Unit | Cost Variability | Notes |
|------|----------|-----------------|-------|
| Natural gas | 100,000/therm | Moderate | Most common, clean |
| Propane | 91,500/gallon | High | Remote areas |
| Fuel oil | 138,500/gallon | High | Backup systems |
| Wood/biomass | 8,000/lb (dry) | Low | Labor intensive |
| Electric | 3,412/kWh | Moderate | Heat pumps only |`
