                        content: `# Keeping Climate Systems Running

Preventive maintenance prevents costly breakdowns and crop losses. Create schedules and stick to them.

## Daily Checks

\`\`\`
□ Walk-through inspection
□ Check temperature/humidity readings
□ Verify fans running
□ Listen for unusual sounds
□ Check for water leaks
□ Review alarm panel
\`\`\`

## Weekly Maintenance

| System | Task |
|--------|------|
| Sensors | Wipe dust, check readings against portable meter |
| Vents | Check operation, lubricate if needed |
| Fans | Check belts, listen for bearing noise |
| Heaters | Visual inspection, check flame color |
| Evap pads | Check water flow, look for algae |
| Controllers | Review data logs for anomalies |

## Monthly Maintenance

| System | Task |
|--------|------|
| HAF fans | Clean blades, check motor |
| Exhaust fans | Clean shutters, check belts |
| Heater filters | Clean or replace |
| Evap pad pump | Check for clogs, clean strainer |
| Curtain systems | Test operation, lubricate tracks |
| Backup systems | Test alarms, backup heaters |

## Seasonal Maintenance

| Season | Focus |
|--------|-------|
| Spring | Cooling system prep, clean glazing |
| Summer | Monitor evap systems, shade check |
| Fall | Heating system prep, seal air leaks |
| Winter | Monitor heating, check for ice damage |

## Sensor Calibration

| Sensor | Calibration Frequency | Method |
|--------|----------------------|--------|
| Temperature | Monthly | Compare to reference thermometer |
| Humidity | Monthly | Salt solution or reference meter |
| CO2 | Quarterly | Calibration gas |
| Light | Annually | Professional calibration |

**Record keeping**: Log all maintenance activities with dates and findings.`
