                        content: `# Maximizing Production Per Square Foot

Vertical farming's value proposition depends on efficient space utilization. Design for density from the start.

## Space Metrics

| Metric | Definition | Target |
|--------|------------|--------|
| Footprint | Floor area occupied | Minimize aisles |
| Growing area | Total plant surface | 3-5x footprint |
| Cubic utilization | % of volume growing | 40-60% |
| Yield/sq ft floor | lbs produced/sq ft | 50-100 lbs/year |

## Level Spacing Factors

| Factor | Consideration |
|--------|---------------|
| Crop height | Final + growing room |
| Light fixture | Depth + clearance |
| Worker access | Hand reach + tools |
| Airflow | Channel space |

**Typical spacing**:
- Microgreens: 8-10"
- Lettuce: 14-18"
- Herbs: 16-20"

## Calculating Growing Density

\`\`\`
Example: 1,000 sq ft building

Traditional greenhouse:
- Growing area: 700 sq ft (aisles, paths)
- Yield: 15 lbs/sq ft/year
- Total: 10,500 lbs/year

4-level vertical farm:
- Growing area: 600 sq ft × 4 = 2,400 sq ft
- Yield: 25 lbs/sq ft/year (LED efficiency)
- Total: 60,000 lbs/year
- 5.7x production increase
\`\`\`

## Layout Design Principles

| Principle | Implementation |
|-----------|----------------|
| Minimize aisles | Mobile racks, reach-in design |
| Maximize height | Use available ceiling |
| Efficient flow | Seed → Harvest linear path |
| Flexible zones | Adjustable shelf heights |

## Common Mistakes

- Too many aisles (wasted space)
- Levels too close (poor airflow)
- Fixed shelf heights (limits crops)
- Ignoring worker ergonomics`
